<title>ISRAEL: SOCCER-ISRAEL AND RUSSIA DRAW 1-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ISRAEL AND RUSSIA DRAW 1-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel and Russia drew 1-1</p>
<p>(halftime 0-0) in a World Cup European Group 5 qualfier on</p>
<p>Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Israel - Gadi Brumer (64th min)</p>
<p>Russia: Igor Kolivanov (79th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 38,000</p>
<p>Group five standings (tabulate under - played, won, drawn,</p>
<p>lost, goals for, against, points):</p>
<p> Russia	     2   1   1   0   5   1   4</p>
<p> Israel	     2   1   1   0   3   2   4</p>
<p> Bulgaria	   2   1   0   1   3   3   3</p>
<p> Luxembourg	 1   0   0   1   1   2   0</p>
<p> Cyprus	     1   0   0   1   0   4   0</p>
<p>Next matches: Nov 10 Cyprus v Israel, Luxembourg v Russia</p>
</text>
